  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following up to activities in the previous biennium, under SSD801, through which a new strategic plan was developed and adopted, activities were undertaken to implement the new strategic plan. These activities pertained to Board reconstitution and capacity development, Re-establishing and capacitating the Secretariat, Membership Development as well as Representation, Alliances and Partnerships. In this context EASS was supported with the development of a communication strategy and various member outreach activities. 
During this Biennium, activities will be undertaken to strengthen the new organization&#x2019;s overall involvement in policy debate as a unified voice. It is thus planned to support EASS with the development of a position paper and advocacy agenda on the business environment. As part of this activity the organization&#x2019;s capacity will also be strengthened to represent the South Sudanese private sectors interests within the overall UN System, as propagated by the recent UN reform. 
In addition, as South Sudanese employers are part of regional bodies of employers, such as the Confederation of IGAD Employers (CIE), activities will also be put towards strengthening their overall participation within this organization, including interaction with the IGAD Secretariat and tackling all topics of interest of employers that require negotiation on regional level, such as labour migration.</narrative>
  </description>
